#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:317
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:319
msgid "Common options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:321
msgid "concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:323 ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:355
msgid "Type: `number`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:324
msgid "Default: `os.cpus().length`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:326
msgid ""
"Specifies the maximum number of concurrent requests from a reader to read"
" directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:328
msgid ""
":book: The higher the number, the higher the performance and load on the "
"file system. If you want to read in quiet mode, set the value to a "
"comfortable number or `1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:334
msgid ""
"In Node, there are [two types of threads][nodejs_thread_pool]: Event Loop"
" (code) and a Thread Pool (fs, dns, …). The thread pool size controlled "
"by the `UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE` environment variable. Its default size is 4 "
"([documentation][libuv_thread_pool]). The pool is one for all tasks "
"within a single Node process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:336
msgid ""
"Any code can make 4 real concurrent accesses to the file system. The rest"
" of the FS requests will wait in the queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:338
msgid ""
":book: Each new instance of FG in the same Node process will use the same"
" Thread pool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:340
msgid ""
"But this package also has the `concurrency` option. This option allows "
"you to control the number of concurrent accesses to the FS at the package"
" level. By default, this package has a value equal to the number of cores"
" available for the current Node process. This allows you to set a value "
"smaller than the pool size (`concurrency: 1`) or, conversely, to prepare "
"tasks for the pool queue more quickly (`concurrency: "
"Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:342
msgid ""
"So, in fact, this package can **only make 4 concurrent requests to the "
"FS**. You can increase this value by using an environment variable "
"(`UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE`), but in practice this does not give a multiple "
"advantage."
msgstr ""

