#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:669
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:671
msgid "What is a static or dynamic pattern?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:673
msgid "All patterns can be divided into two types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:675
msgid ""
"**static**. A pattern is considered static if it can be used to get an "
"entry on the file system without using matching mechanisms. For example, "
"the `file.js` pattern is a static pattern because we can just verify that"
" it exists on the file system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:676
msgid ""
"**dynamic**. A pattern is considered dynamic if it cannot be used "
"directly to find occurrences without using a matching mechanisms. For "
"example, the `*` pattern is a dynamic pattern because we cannot use this "
"pattern directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:678
msgid ""
"A pattern is considered dynamic if it contains the following characters "
"(`…` — any characters or their absence) or options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:680
msgid "The [`caseSensitiveMatch`](#casesensitivematch) option is disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:681
msgid "`\\\\` (the escape character)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:682
msgid "`*`, `?`, `!` (at the beginning of line)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:683
msgid "`[…]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:684
msgid "`(…|…)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:685
msgid ""
"`@(…)`, `!(…)`, `*(…)`, `?(…)`, `+(…)` (respects the "
"[`extglob`](#extglob) option)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:686
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`{…,…}`, `{…..…}` (respects the [`braceExpansion`](#braceexpansion) "
"option)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:688
msgid "How to write patterns on Windows?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:690
msgid ""
"Always use forward-slashes in glob expressions (patterns and "
"[`ignore`](#ignore) option). Use backslashes for escaping characters. "
"With the [`cwd`](#cwd) option use a convenient format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:692
msgid "**Bad**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:701
msgid "**Good**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:710
msgid ""
":book: Use the [`.convertPathToPattern`](#convertpathtopatternpath) "
"package to convert Windows-style path to a Unix-style path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:712
msgid "Read more about [matching with backslashes][micromatch_backslashes]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:714
msgid "Why are parentheses match wrong?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:725
msgid "Refers to Bash. You need to escape special characters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:731
msgid ""
"Read more about [matching special characters as "
"literals][picomatch_matching_special_characters_as_literals]. Or use the "
"[`.escapePath`](#escapepathpath)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:733
msgid "How to exclude directory from reading?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:735
msgid ""
"You can use a negative pattern like this: `!**/node_modules` or "
"`!**/node_modules/**`. Also you can use [`ignore`](#ignore) option. Just "
"look at the example below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:744
msgid ""
"If you don't want to read the `second` directory, you must write the "
"following pattern: `!**/second` or `!**/second/**`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:751
msgid ""
":warning: When you write `!**/second/**/*` it means that the directory "
"will be **read**, but all the entries will not be included in the "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:753
msgid ""
"You have to understand that if you write the pattern to exclude "
"directories, then the directory will not be read under any circumstances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:755
msgid "How to use UNC path?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fast-glob_README.md:757
msgid ""
"You cannot use [Uniform Naming Convention (UNC)][unc_path] paths as "
"patterns (due to syntax) directly, but you can use them as [`cwd`](#cwd) "
"directory or use the `fg.convertPathToPattern` method."
msgstr ""

